    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Inverse proportion occurs when one variable increases while the other decreases at a reciprocal rate. This is expressed as <em>y = k/x</em> or <em>y ∝ 1/x</em>, where <strong>k</strong> is the constant of proportionality. The graph is a reciprocal curve (hyperbola) that never touches the x or y axes.</p>",
